  "instance_name": "general_custer_battle_of_little_bighorn",
  "label": "Battle of Little Bighorn",
  "description": "The Battle of Little Bighorn, fought in 1876, was a decisive victory for Native American forces led by Sitting Bull and Crazy Horse against the 7th Cavalry Regiment of the U.S. Army, commanded by General George Armstrong Custer. This battle is central to the meme's context, as it is the historical event that links Custer to Native American conflict, allowing the meme to use his image to symbolize violent aggression toward Native Americans. The defeat of Custer at Little Bighorn is a well-known historical event that provides the basis for the meme's juxtaposition of hatred toward both banks and Native Americans.",
